  "instructions": [
    "Preheat oven to 400°F (200°C).",
    "Roll out empanada pastry dough to 1/4 inch thickness.",
    "Cut out circles of dough using a cookie cutter or the rim of a glass.",
    "In a bowl, mix together ground beef, onion, garlic, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Place a tablespoon of beef mixture in the center of each dough circle.",
    "Brush edges with beaten egg and fold dough in half to form a half-circle.",
    "Press edges to seal and use a fork to crimp.",
    "Brush tops with warm water and place on a baking sheet.",
    "Bake for 20-25 minutes, or until golden brown.",
    "Serve warm and enjoy!"
